    "title": "A=1 shape-A coefficient syzygy-bundle cubic splitting",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "the coefficient linear series has only degree-one, -two, and -three minimal syzygies",
    "statement": "Let V be the r-dimensional basepoint-free parameter coefficient space of the Shape-A biform, of degree m=e-2. Its evaluation bundle kernel E on P1 splits geometrically as a sum of O(-mu_i). The three-class identity S_2 V=S_(m+2) makes H^1(E(2)) vanish, so every mu_i is in {1,2,3}. If c_j counts degree-j summands, then c_1+c_2+c_3=r-1, c_1+2c_2+3c_3=m, and 2c_1+c_2=3r-(e+1). The inverse prolongation J has dimension c_1. At the earlier three-source-class rank bound 61083979322, exactly two conditional profiles occur: (1,0,61083979320) and (0,2,61083979319); the locator-interpolation rank amplification subsequently excludes that boundary. A nonzero common source-Gram matrix forces c_1>0, and generally c_1>=max(0,2r-(n+2)).",
